<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="Privacy information for RedRiverGorgeHiker.com, including optional Google Analytics and Pinterest measurement."
>
  <div class="page prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p><small>Last updated: August 19, 2026</small></p>

    <section>
      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>RedRiverGorgeHiker.com is operated by Red River Gorge Hiker LLC under the Red River Gorge Hiker brand. It is a static photography and outdoor-interest website. It does not create visitor accounts, run its own online shopping cart, or directly collect payment-card information.</p>
      <p>GitHub Pages and ordinary internet infrastructure may process standard technical information needed to deliver and secure the site. Optional measurement tools are described below.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Google Analytics</h2>
      <p>Red River Gorge Hiker uses Google Analytics 4 (GA4) for optional website measurement. The purpose is to understand website traffic and usage, understand traffic sources, improve the site, evaluate marketing campaigns, and measure actions such as outbound clicks to Fine Art America.</p>
      <p>Depending on how a visitor uses the site, Google Analytics may process information such as page views and site interactions; referring source or campaign information, including UTM campaign parameters; outbound-link activity; approximate geographic information such as country, region or state, and city; browser, device, and related technical information; and pseudonymous first-party Analytics identifiers or cookies used to distinguish visits and users.</p>
      <p>These Analytics identifiers do not tell Red River Gorge Hiker a visitor’s name, and Red River Gorge Hiker does not use GA4 to identify individual visitors by name.</p>
      <p>Google processes Analytics information on behalf of Red River Gorge Hiker for website measurement and analytics purposes. Google Analytics may use IP-address information during collection for functions such as routing, spam detection, and deriving approximate geographic information. Google states that GA4 discards raw IP addresses after this collection-time use and before Analytics data is logged. Red River Gorge Hiker does not receive or store visitors’ raw IP addresses through GA4.</p>
      <p>For more information about Google’s processing when websites use Google services such as Google Analytics, see <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Pinterest measurement</h2>
      <p>Red River Gorge Hiker also uses the Pinterest Tag for optional website measurement. The purpose is to understand Pinterest-driven visits, evaluate Pinterest campaigns, and support Pinterest advertising measurement and audience reporting.</p>
      <p>When enabled, the Pinterest Tag may process information about page visits, referral or campaign information, browser and device information, and Pinterest-related first-party identifiers or storage used for measurement. Pinterest may use this information to attribute website activity to Pinterest advertising or engagement and to provide campaign and audience reporting.</p>
      <p>Red River Gorge Hiker does not enable Pinterest Enhanced Match and does not send visitor email addresses or hashed email addresses through the Pinterest Tag.</p>
      <p>For more information about Pinterest’s privacy practices, see <a href="https://policy.pinterest.com/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pinterest’s Privacy Policy<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Analytics choice</h2>
      <p>Analytics storage is denied by default. Google Analytics and Pinterest measurement are configured as optional. Measurement does not load until a visitor selects <strong>Allow analytics</strong>. Selecting <strong>Decline</strong> keeps these tools disabled on later page loads. The site stores the visitor’s analytics preference in local browser storage so the choice can be remembered.</p>
      <p>For a simple and privacy-protective implementation, Red River Gorge Hiker applies this consent choice to all visitors rather than attempting to determine which visitors are located in the European Economic Area, United Kingdom, or Switzerland. Visitors can reopen the choice at any time using <strong>Analytics choices</strong> in the website footer.</p>
      <p>For Google Analytics, advertising-related Consent Mode settings remain denied. This implementation does not add Meta Pixel, Roku tracking pixels, Google Ads remarketing, advertising personalization, Google Tag Manager, or Pinterest Enhanced Match.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Email</h2>
      <p>If you email Ryan at Ryan@RedRiverGorgeHiker.com, the information you choose to provide may be retained by Red River Gorge Hiker LLC when reasonably useful for responding to your message, administering the business, or maintaining ordinary business records.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Fine Art America</h2>
      <p>Online purchases are completed on Fine Art America. Fine Art America handles the account, checkout, payment, order, shipping, and transaction information submitted through its service. Fine Art America has its own privacy practices, which apply when you visit or purchase through that service.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>Privacy questions may be sent to Ryan@RedRiverGorgeHiker.com.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
